*.fasl
*~
# Emacs autosave (#foo#) and lock (.#foo) files.  This was `#*#', which
# git read as a COMMENT -- a pattern starting with # needs the `**/'
# prefix (house form, also matches at any depth) or a backslash.
# Audit 2026-08-16.
**/#*#
.#*
*.dx64fsl
*.lx64fsl
# npm belongs to /projects/apps/tailwind, NOT to this repo.  The shared
# build compiles css/demos-style.css from apps/tailwind/demos-input.css,
# whose @source line already scans ../../demos/**, so every demo here --
# naca-nurbs included -- is registered by existing, and none of them
# needs a toolchain of its own.  Deploy hosts never run npm; the
# compiled css is committed.
#
# node_modules/ stays as a guard in case someone runs npm in here by
# habit.  `package-lock.json' was ALSO listed and has been removed: a
# lockfile appearing under demos/ means a second, unregistered tailwind
# setup is growing, which is exactly what happened in
# naca-nurbs/tailwind/ (a 40KB lockfile with no package.json beside it,
# deleted 2026-08-16).  Better that it shows up as untracked and gets
# noticed than that it is silently ignored.
node_modules/
system-index.txt

